			"notes": "Obama IP Checker v1.0.0 adds server-side IP history, shared-address lookups, and IP bans for Fabric.\n\n- `/ip <username|UUID>` shows recorded addresses, timestamps, previous names, and players sharing each address.\n- `/ip <IPv4|IPv6>` shows the recorded players using that address.\n- `/banip <username|UUID|IP>` bans the selected address or every recorded address for an account, and disconnects affected online players.\n- Commands require operator level 3/admin permission. History is saved as readable per-player JSON under `ip-checker/players/`.\n- IPv6 socket parsing is corrected so the mod's IPv6 bans reject connections before play login.\n\nSupported stable game versions: **1.21.11, 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2, 26.2, 26.3**.\nSupported 26.4 snapshots: **snapshot-1, snapshot-2, snapshot-3, snapshot-4**.\n\nInstall **one jar matching your exact Minecraft version**, together with Fabric Loader 0.19.5+ and the matching Fabric API dependency from the [install guide](https://github.com/ObamaEssentials/IPChecker/blob/v1.0.0/README.md). Java 21+ is required for 1.21.11; Java 25+ for 26.x. Clients need no mod.\n\nThe all-versions ZIP contains every mod jar, the guide, license, verification results, and SHA-256 checksums. Individual jars are also attached below.\n\nReleases follow **plugin versions** (`v1.0.0`). Each supported game version has its own source branch named after that version. The `main` branch contains the complete build matrix.\n\nValidation: all ten builds and their unit tests passed. All ten packaged variants passed dedicated local server checks. Real local protocol clients verified IPv4/IPv6 join logging, command permissions, private lookups between operators, shared-IP disconnection, and banned reconnection on 1.21.11 and 26.1. Production and proxy setups were not tested; future snapshots require another matching build.\n\nMIT licensed."
		}
